  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a twenty-four-song set at the Cow Haus in Talahassee, Florida, on Friday, February 6, 1998 [1][5]. This recording, documented as the eighteenth of 467 archived shows for the performer, captures a full eighty-one-minute performance [1][5]. The lineup includes several rare tracks, such as “Raid On Entebbe,” “Tulsa Imperative,” and “West Country Dream,” alongside four songs appearing for the first time in the archive: “We Were Patriots,” “Waving At You,” “Family Happiness,” and “Third Snow Song” [1][5]. The set also features the mythically rare “Tell Me On A Sunday,” which has only two archived performances [5]. Taped by Jon Nall and transferred by Brian Eck, the audio is widely praised by listeners for its quality given the era [1][2][3]. One reviewer, nigelewan, called the recording quality wonderful and identified “Orange Ball Of Hate” as their favorite version of the song [2]. Another listener, delusionaldiminutive, noted the sound was great, though they observed the first three songs were quite quiet [3]. Mattgee, an avid fan, described this as the best live recording they have ever heard, highlighting the energy on “Tulsa Imperative,” “West Country Dream,” and “Family Happiness” [4]. Despite a slightly low volume, the setlist’s mix of older tunes and rarities makes this a highly recommended listen [2][4].",
